#
# Counter-example: a general math:CellComplex (NOT simplicial) whose codimension-2
# (coface cX, far-face aZ) group has a single boundary composition of sign product +1,
# so the finite signed sum Σ_b [cX:b]·[b:aZ] = +1 ≠ 0 — ∂∘∂ ≠ 0. It fires
# math:GeneralBoundarySquareZeroConstraint (the logic:JoinAggregateConstraint,
# shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent → math:BrokenBoundarySquareZero) and NO other finding:
# it is a plain math:CellComplex (so the simplicial diamond constraint does not target
# it) and every math:CellIncidence carries its coface, face, and ±1 sign.

@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/general-cw-broken/> .

ex:broken a math:CellComplex ;
    math:hasCell ex:cX , ex:bY , ex:aZ .

ex:dim0 a math:NaturalNumber ; math:inNumberSystem math:naturalNumbers ; math:isExact true .
ex:dim1 a math:NaturalNumber ; math:inNumberSystem math:naturalNumbers ; math:isExact true .
ex:dim2 a math:NaturalNumber ; math:inNumberSystem math:naturalNumbers ; math:isExact true .

ex:cX a math:Cell ; math:cellDimension ex:dim2 .
ex:bY a math:Cell ; math:cellDimension ex:dim1 .
ex:aZ a math:Cell ; math:cellDimension ex:dim0 .

# The single boundary composition cX ▷ bY ▷ aZ with product (+1)·(+1) = +1, unpaired:
# the group (cX, aZ) sums to +1 ≠ 0.
ex:incCXbY a math:CellIncidence ; math:incidenceCoface ex:cX ; math:incidenceFace ex:bY ; math:incidenceSign 1 .
ex:incbYaZ a math:CellIncidence ; math:incidenceCoface ex:bY ; math:incidenceFace ex:aZ ; math:incidenceSign 1 .
